        "summary": "Expiry: the granted run time is down to seconds, so no check, experiment or record can be added or revised — the named submission is the already-validated, unmodified draft, whose last acceptance was recorded as no_change. The run's preserved work stands as submitted, with receipts, knowledge and scoped limits for four findings: (1) the actor layer's event egress parks the loop on an unconsumed bounded channel and, once enough nodes park, the cluster stops deciding, measured at capacities 8, 64 and the shipped default 1024 under the corrected per-destination transport, with the superseded transport-jam run retained as an excluded cause and a 21.69s retrospective bound (receipts ff4511e8, 76557a28, bbff5b4c); (2) the core has no timer-driven repair for a lost Accepted reply — the leader's own acceptance plus nothing, heartbeats only afterwards, progress returning with a later proposal — measured at two and three nodes with quorum-critical losses (receipts 092538c6, 9f3f25cc); (3) append_notify can resolve Ok for an index occupied by another entry, with the Superseded heuristic shadowed by the index-first arm, bounded by measurement to entries the following leader did not adopt while the adopted case is truthful (receipts 743518e2, 78c53df3); (4) the actor layer owns the instance but exposes no compaction path, with the fatal write error's panic inside the actor task surfacing to callers only as Shutdown (source-settled). One measurement is explicitly unfinished and recorded as that question's next discriminator rather than as a claim: driving a Storage whose write returns Err through the actor to see whether the actor really dies and whether every endpoint collapses to Shutdown."
